ack-and-forth  subject my daughter said to me dad I  know who Shakespeare was I said really  who she said he was the man who wrote  those plays mystery solved all we need  to know about him is the stories he told  and how they move us beyond that he was  a man like any other man only more so  this same daughter by the way once  summoned me to her room at bedtime and  asked point-blank dad Adam and Eve true  or false that was not long after her  sister Isabel cried in desperation dad  Jesus was Jewish proving that sometimes  stories overlap in ways that are  contradictory but enriching one of my  favorite movies when I was a kid was the  1959 Ben Hur I eventually saw an earlier  version from 1925 the silence scratched  bleached black-and-white images  convinced me for a moment that it was  actual footage of a chariot race from  the Roman Empire it all looks so remote  so genuine it was only a few moments  later not without disappointment that I  returned to my ruthless senses and  accepted that the plebeians and the  bleachers were extras from the San  Fernando Valley their clothing  manufactured in Culver City their  sandals in Reseda their Latin a little  bit more than rusty every year when I  ride for this evening I think of a  charismatic general who was a character  in a screenplay that won the nickel the  night that Anton was here I don't  remember the name of that very fine  script but remember that general it  still makes me a little sad that he died  at the end of that story I'd rather  think he might have retired to Sardinia  instead the sheer pain in the ass of  writing a story his only overcome by the  sheer delight of telling it there really  is nothing more fun than you can do with  your clothes on then hearing a story  well told when a good story touches you  it becomes indestructible  and so storytellers themselves are  indestructible congratulation to you  guys and gals our winners tonight  you have contributed to an endlessly  flowing tradition the 